01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
A Knight's Tale is a 2001 American medieval action comedy film
written, co-produced and directed by Brian Helgeland.

12
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The film stars Heath Ledger as William Thatcher, a peasant squire who poses as a knight and competes in tournaments, winning accolades and
acquiring friendships with such historical figures as Edward the Black Prince (James Purefoy) and Geoffrey Chaucer (Paul Bettany).

13
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
Its 14th-century story is intentionally anachronistic, with many modern pop
culture references and a soundtrack featuring 1970s music.

14
01:38:00,000 --> 01:38:06,000
The film takes its name from Chaucer's story "The Knight's Tale", part of The
Canterbury Tales, and also draws several plot points from Chaucer's work.

15
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
A Knight's Tale was released by Columbia Pictures in
the United States on May 11, 2001.

16
01:52:00,000 --> 01:52:06,000
It received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $117.5
million against a budget of $65 million.

17
01:59:00,000 --> 01:59:06,000
The film explores themes of london, england,
poetry, rivalry, sword fight, knight.

18
02:06:00,000 --> 02:06:06,000
The tone is emotional.
